      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "James St. John",
      "description": "Quartzose sandstones in the Cambrian of Minnesota, USA.\nThis cliff exposure consists of quartzose sandstones of the Mazomanie Formation, a shallow marine siliciclastic succession in the Upper Cambrian of the Upper Mississippi Valley, USA.  Herringbone cross-bedding and trough cross-bedding are moderately common here.  Skolithos trace fossils and intraclastic sandstone horizons are also present.\nStratigraphy: Mazomanie Formation, upper Tunnel City Group (formerly the Franconia Sandstone), Sunwaptan Stage, Upper Cambrian, ~491-493 Ma\n\nLocality: riverside cliff exposures along the western side of St. Croix River, below a rest stop along Rt. 95 between mileposts 101 and 102, just northeast of Lookout Point, north-northeast of the town of Stillwater, Minnesota, USA (45° 05’ 03.80\" North, 92° 47’ 10.33\" West)",
      "dateCreated": "2015-06-04 15:54",
